{"version":"0.1","documentType":"opinion","source":{"kind":"lrb_html","caseId":"2015_01557","path":"../miranda/opinions/coa/2015/2015_01557.htm","publicationStatus":"published"},"header":{"title":"People v Cooke","slipOpinion":"2015 NY Slip Op 01557","officialCitation":"24 NY3d 1196","court":"Court of Appeals","decisionDate":"2015-02-24"},"appearances":[],"opinions":[{"kind":"majority","author":null,"label":null,"joiners":[],"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"page_marker","text":"{**24 NY3d at 1197}","citation":"24 NY3d at 1197"},{"type":"text","text":" OPINION OF THE COURT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"page_marker","text":"{**24 NY3d at 1197}","citation":"24 NY3d at 1197"},{"type":"text","text":" OPINION OF THE COURT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Memorandum."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The order of the Appellate Division should be affirmed."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The trial court's failure to make a finding of necessity for the stun belt's use does "},{"type":"text","text":"not constitute an unwaivable mode of proceedings error ("},{"type":"link","href":"../2009/2009_05367.htm","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"see People v Buchanan"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 13 NY3d 1"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 4 [2009]; "},{"type":"link","href":"../2013/2013_02106.htm","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"see generally People v Hanley"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 20 NY3d 601"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 604 [2013]; "},{"type":"link","href":"../2013/2013_05415.htm","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"People v Schrock"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 108 AD3d 1221"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 1224-1225 [4th Dept 2013], "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"lv denied"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 22 NY3d 998 [2013],"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":" denied reconsideration"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 23 NY3d 1025 [2014]; "},{"type":"link","href":"../2012/2012_00858.htm","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"see also People v Gamble"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 18 NY3d 386"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 396-397 [2012], "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"rearg denied"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 19 NY3d 833 [2012]). Thus, as defendant never objected, and indeed expressly consented to wearing a stun belt at trial, he waived his contention that he was denied a fair trial on the ground that he was restrained by means of that security device ("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"see People v Iannone"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 45 NY2d 589, 600 [1978]; "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"cf. Buchanan"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 13 NY3d at 3). We have considered defendant's remaining contentions and find them to be without merit."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Chief Judge Lippman and Judges Read, Pigott, Rivera, Abdus-Salaam and Stein concur; Judge Fahey taking no part."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"On review of submissions pursuant to section 500.11 of the Rules of the Court of Appeals (22 NYCRR 500.11), order affirmed, in a memorandum."}],"provenance":{"startLine":7,"endLine":19}}]}],"footnotes":[],"disposition":{"text":"On review of submissions pursuant to section 500.11 of the Rules of the Court of Appeals (22 NYCRR 500.11), order affirmed, in a memorandum.","provenance":{"startLine":19,"endLine":19}},"renderingHints":{"hasOfficialPageMarkers":true,"hasAppearances":false,"hasFootnotes":false,"hasSeparateOpinions":false},"debug":{"diagnostics":[]}}
